page('story.html','A life of curiosity and care',head('About Steven','A life of curiosity<br>and care.','Husband, father, friend. An engineer with a designer’s eye, a writer’s imagination, and a way of helping people move forward.')+'''<div class="reading-layout"><aside class="reading-sidebar" aria-label="About Steven"><p class="eyebrow">A few ways to know him</p><a href="#family">Family</a><a href="#making">Making things</a><a href="#others">Making time for others</a><a href="timeline.html">Moments through the years →</a><a href="memories.html">Everyone’s memories →</a></aside><article class="prose"><figure><img src="assets/steven-schrembeck-family.jpg" alt="Steven with Amanda and their two sons by the ocean" width="720" height="407"><figcaption>Steven, Amanda, and their boys.</figcaption></figure><h2 id="family">At the heart of his life.</h2><p>Steven was Amanda’s husband and a father to their two sons. This collection is for them, for the people who knew him, and for anyone who comes to know him through the words, work, and memories gathered here.</p><p>He passed away in September 2026. There is more to a life than any page can hold. These are some of the pieces people have kept.</p><h2 id="making">A mind that kept making.</h2><p>A UI developer and Principal Engineer at Cox Automotive, Steven cared about how things worked and how people experienced them. His interests reached beyond software: he wrote <em>A Different Compass</em>, recorded <em>Reality 101</em>, created audio fiction through <em>Collected</em>, and explored ideas on his <em>Seeking Minima</em> channel.</p><p>He also kept trying things. Rodrigo Martinez remembers the care Steven put into an experiment with a plant-based food service, Joyfull Foods. It was far from his day-to-day work, and that was part of what Rodrigo admired about it.</p><blockquote><p>“If you say it matters, i’ll make it happen..”</p></blockquote><p class="small muted">Steven, remembered by Winnie Widastra, on the icon styling.</p><h2 id="others">Making time for others.</h2><p>Again and again, the memories return to his generosity: answering a question, making an introduction, encouraging someone early in their career, or simply offering to help.</p><blockquote><p>“He never not offered to help.”</p></blockquote><p class="small muted">Mansi Demla</p><p>Vivian Milender remembers how he encouraged people to explore and ask questions. Hudson Akridge remembers his colorful glasses and willingness to speak his truth. Others remember the humor, the conversations, and the confidence he helped them find.</p><p>Every memory adds something. Together, they leave room for the many ways people knew Steven.</p><p><a href="memories.html">Read the shared memories →</a></p><aside class="support"><p>For Steven’s family</p><p>The original remembrance links to Amanda’s fundraiser for the family. <a href="https://www.gofundme.com/f/support-stevens-wife-and-sons">Visit the family’s GoFundMe ↗</a></p></aside><div class="source-note">This introduction draws on the original memorial and the supplied collection of friends’ and colleagues’ recollections. Individual memories remain attributed to their contributors. <a href="memories.html">Explore the collection</a>.</div></article></div>''','story.html')
items=[('2016','Words that stayed','Anthony remembers something Steven said in a talk: “You get what you tolerate.”','Anthony','memory-1790788089496-r98cdc'),('2018','Always trying something','Rodrigo remembers Joyfull Foods, Steven’s plant-based food service experiment, and the commitment he brought to making it right.','Rodrigo Martinez (Roddy)','memory-1790790317668-rnjhm6'),('2021','An offer to help','Mansi remembers his smile and his willingness to help. Jeff remembers a question about machine learning becoming an introduction. Clay remembers his humor.','Mansi Demla, Jeff Cameron, and Clay Elrod','memory-1790858752833-fmj414'),('2022','Away from the office','A birthday party. Dad friends. Steven asking whether both his boys could come.','Jeff Cameron','memory-jn3p6ts'),('2023','Care in the details','Winnie remembers an exchange about icon styling: “If you say it matters, i’ll make it happen..”','Winnie Widastra','memory-1790865438289-qow71h'),('2024','Room to grow','Vivian remembers a kind colleague who encouraged people early in their careers to explore and ask questions.','Vivian Milender','memory-1790944279023-4ohqhj'),('2025–2026','Ideas worth sharing','Jason remembers Steven’s unusual and thought-provoking workplace presentations. Saved recordings are dated September 24, 2025 and January 6, 2026.','Jason Antman and recording metadata','memory-1790790861216-jqqhyd'),('2026','A different way of seeing','Hudson remembers the colorful glasses, Steven’s brightness, and his willingness to speak his truth.','Hudson Akridge','memory-1790790304809-pmhy5a')]
page('timeline.html','Moments through the years',head('From the shared memories','Moments through<br>the years.','Small moments from different lives that crossed Steven’s. A growing picture, told by the people who were there.')+'<div class="timeline">'+''.join(f'<section class="timeline-item"><div class="timeline-year">{year}</div><div><h2>{e(title)}</h2><p>{e(text)}</p><p class="small muted" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12px;margin-top:18px">Remembered by {e(by)}</p><a class="text-link" href="memories.html#{anchor}">Read the memory →</a></div></section>' for year,title,text,by,anchor in items)+'</div><p class="source-note">Dates generally follow contributors’ own recollections. Presentation dates follow the saved recording metadata, which differs from one contributor’s event-year attribution. This is a collection of moments, not a complete biography.</p>','story.html')
