page('index.html','The Steven Schrembeck archive',f'''<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">The Steven Schrembeck archive</p><h1 id="hero-title"><span>Steven</span><span>Schrembeck.</span></h1><p class="hero-subtitle">His words. His work.<br>A place to return to.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="collection.html">Explore the archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="story.html">About Steven <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-note">For everyone who knew him.<br>And everyone who has yet to discover him.</p></div><figure class="hero-photo"><img src="assets/steven-schrembeck-family.jpg" alt="Steven with Amanda and their two sons by the ocean" width="720" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption class="caption"><span>Steven, Amanda, and their boys.</span><a href="photos.html">The photographs ↗</a></figcaption></figure></section><nav class="routes" aria-label="Explore the collections"><a class="route" href="work.html#writing"><span class="route-num">01</span><span><span class="route-title">Read his writing</span><span class="route-sub">A Different Compass</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="route" href="collection.html?type=audio"><span class="route-num">02</span><span><span class="route-title">Hear his voice</span><span class="route-sub">Podcasts, stories, and conversations</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="route" href="collection.html?type=video"><span class="route-num">03</span><span><span class="route-title">See his ideas</span><span class="route-sub">Seeking Minima and beyond</span></span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav><section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Begin anywhere</p><h2>A mind worth exploring.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="collection.html">The complete collection →</a></div><div class="work-list"><a class="work-row" href="writing/it-s-connection.html"><div><small>A Different Compass · October 2025</small><h3>It’s Connection</h3><p>A piece of writing to begin with.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="items/{item_id('collected/001-reverie.mp3')}.html"><div><small>Collected · Audio fiction</small><h3>Reverie</h3><p>Step into an imagined world.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="collection.html?type=video"><div><small>Seeking Minima · 22 saved videos</small><h3>Questions worth following</h3><p>Technology, meaning, and being human.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="work-row" href="timeline.html"><div><small>A chronology of the content</small><h3>The work, through time</h3><p>Follow the threads across the years.</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section><section class="voice"><div><p class="eyebrow">In his own voice</p><h2>Spend a little time<br>with Steven.</h2><p>Listen to his introduction to Reality 101. The saved recording is right here, with its original source and transcript.</p><a class="text-link" href="collection.html?type=audio">Explore the recordings →</a></div><div class="voice-player"><div class="recording"><img src="assets/reality-cover.jpg" alt="Reality 101 artwork" width="72" height="72"><div><small>REALITY 101 · INTRODUCTION</small><h3>Surprise, you can learn how it all works</h3><small>1 min 49 sec</small></div></div><audio controls preload="none" aria-label="Reality 101 introduction"><source src="recordings/reality-101-introduction.mp3" type="audio/mpeg"></audio><p class="audio-note"><a href="items/{item_id('reality/003-trailer-surprise-you-can-learn-how-it-all-works.mp3')}.html">Saved file, original source &amp; transcript →</a></p></div></section><section class="section story-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Behind the work</p><h2 style="margin-top:16px">A different way<br>of seeing.</h2><div class="portrait-label"><img src="assets/steven-schrembeck.jpg" alt="Steven in his green glasses" width="62" height="62" loading="lazy"><div>Engineer. Writer. Storyteller.<span>Husband, father, and friend.</span></div></div></div><div class="story-prose"><p>Steven was a UI developer and Principal Engineer at Cox Automotive. Beyond software, he wrote, made audio fiction, recorded podcasts, and shared explorations on video.</p><p>This archive brings those pieces together, so his family, friends, colleagues, and future readers can keep discovering the things he made.</p><a class="text-link" href="story.html">About Steven →</a></div></section><section class="preserve"><div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:12px">Made to be kept</p><h2>Find a file. Keep a piece.</h2><p>Download individual works or keep a complete copy. Original sources remain alongside the saved files.</p></div><a class="button secondary" href="files.html">Browse downloads <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></section>''')
page('story.html','About Steven',head('The person behind the work','About Steven.','Engineer. Writer. Storyteller. Husband, father, and friend.')+'''<div class="reading-layout"><aside class="reading-sidebar"><img src="assets/steven-schrembeck.jpg" alt="Steven in his green glasses" width="260" height="227"><p style="margin-top:14px">Steven Schrembeck</p></aside><article class="prose"><p>Steven Schrembeck was a UI developer and Principal Engineer at Cox Automotive. He was Amanda’s husband and a father to their two sons. He passed away in September 2026.</p><p>His creative work ranged across essays, podcasts, audio fiction, and video. <em>A Different Compass</em>, <em>Reality 101</em>, <em>Collected</em>, and <em>Seeking Minima</em> are different ways into his interests and imagination.</p><h2>A home for the work.</h2><p>This archive brings together saved copies of the things he made and shared, alongside links to their original sources. It is for his family, for the people who knew him, and for anyone who finds something here worth spending time with.</p><p><a href="collection.html">Explore the collection →</a></p><h2>Remembering the person.</h2><p>The people who knew Steven have their own stories to tell. Their remembrances belong to them, and help put the work in context.</p><div class="remembrance-link"><p class="eyebrow">A personal remembrance</p><h3><a href="https://remembering-steven-schrembeck.opzero.sh/">Remembering Steven Schrembeck ↗</a></h3><p class="small muted">By Jeff Cameron · Read the original post</p></div><p><a href="memories.html">Memories shared by friends and colleagues →</a></p><div class="source-note">Biographical details come from the original memorial and supplied collection. This introduction does not attempt a complete biography.</div></article></div>''','story.html')
